  "verdict": "ADVANCED_NOT_VALIDATED: the backbone-path topological rigidity descriptor is the first structure-only, non-circular model to beat both the incumbent ML (LOO 35.7 vs 39.1 C) and the leave-one-out NULL (37.0 C), improving the best LOO MAE from 40.5 to 35.7 C and correctly ranking the two highest-Tg systems (DDS 208, IPDA 158) that whole-molecule aromatic fraction cannot separate. It still FAILS the >=25 C KPI gate (G2) and the n>=12 data gate (G1). Connectivity alone cannot capture IPDA's gem-dimethyl STERIC rigidity (B low, Tg high) -> the remaining constraints are (a) protocol-consistent data quantity and (b) a steric/side-group descriptor beyond backbone connectivity. NOT a Phase-0 promotion."
